---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { pageByPath } from '../../lib/pages';
import { articleJsonLd } from '../../lib/jsonld';

const page = pageByPath('/terms/')!;
---
<Base title={page.title} description={page.description} path={page.path} jsonLd={[articleJsonLd(page)]}>
  <h1>Terms of use</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    B4WeMeet is operated as a free, independent, non-commercial project provided "as is" and "as available", with no
    commercial support, service-level agreement (SLA), advertising, or sponsorships.
  </p>
  <p><small>Effective / last updated: November 23, 2026</small></p>

  <h2>General interview guidance only</h2>
  <p>
    The guides, question libraries, example answers, templates, and Prep Pack Builder on B4WeMeet are for general
    informational purposes only. Nothing on this site is employment, career, HR, or legal advice. Every employer runs
    interviews differently, and B4WeMeet makes no guarantee regarding any employer's interview process, questions, or
    hiring outcomes.
  </p>

  <h2>Your local data and backups</h2>
  <p>
    Everything you enter in the Prep Pack Builder is stored locally in your browser (IndexedDB) on your device.
    B4WeMeet has no user accounts, cloud sync, or server-side copy of your prep. You are solely responsible for
    securing access to your device, exporting and storing your own backup files safely, and understanding that
    clearing site data in your browser will erase your locally stored prep.
  </p>

  <h2>Bring-your-own AI (BYO-AI)</h2>
  <p>
    Optional handoff features copy your prep pack to your clipboard and open third-party AI services such as ChatGPT
    or Claude in a new tab. Those services are operated by third parties under their own terms of service and privacy
    policies. You are responsible for reviewing those terms and deciding what information to paste into any
    third-party AI tool.
  </p>

  <h2>Independence and trademarks</h2>
  <p>
    B4WeMeet is an independent project and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by OpenAI, Anthropic, or
    any named employers, platforms, or organizations. All third-party product names, service names, and trademarks
    belong to their respective owners.
  </p>

  <h2>Permitted and prohibited use</h2>
  <p>
    B4WeMeet is free for personal or workplace use at your own risk. You agree not to:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Abuse, disrupt, overload, or attempt to interfere with the site or its hosting infrastructure.</li>
    <li>Engage in wholesale commercial republishing, repackaging, or reselling of the site's guides, question libraries, or templates.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Provided "as is" — no warranties</h2>
  <p>
    B4WeMeet and all content and tools on it are provided <strong>"as is"</strong> and{' '}
    <strong>"as available"</strong>, without warranties of any kind, whether express or implied, including without
    limitation implied warranties of accuracy, completeness, merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or
    non-infringement.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent permitted by law, B4WeMeet and its operators are not liable for any direct, indirect,
    incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages — including loss of locally stored data, device issues,
    third-party AI service outputs, or hiring and employment outcomes — arising out of or related to your use of or
    reliance on this site.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes and privacy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update or discontinue parts of the site or revise these Terms at any time. Continued use after changes are
    posted constitutes acceptance of the updated Terms. Please also review our{' '}
    <a href="/privacy/">Security and Privacy</a> page.
  </p>
</Base>
